# Every file here is read by bash, jq, grep or node, which take a carriage
# return as part of the line: a CRLF checkout (Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true) turns each hook into a silent no-op (they fail open)
# and every guard pattern into one that never matches. Claude Code installs a
# plugin with a git clone, so the cache inherits that checkout too. LF on
# every platform, whatever the clone's own setting.
* text=auto eol=lf
